IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `gas-types`

-- Gas Act 1986 (UK) — GOAL 3: CONSUMER REDRESS ORDERS AND RESALE PRICES
-- (ss 30G, 30K, 30M-30O, 37).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1986-44.txt.
-- The consumer asks: "My supplier broke a licence condition and I lost out.
-- Can a consumer redress order still be made; by when must I be paid, and
-- does interest run if I am not; how much can be ordered in all? And if gas
-- was resold to me above the maximum price, what can I recover?"

§ `Goal 3 — redress and resale`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days on from` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- "N months from" a day: the corresponding date N months on, or the last day
-- of that month where it has none (F5).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months from` d MEANS `add months` d n

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE DATE, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `served on or before` m `the date` d IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST x  THEN x AT MOST d

-- s 30K(3): the s 30I(1) notice must be served on or after the confirmation
-- or making of the order, and within the months that follow it (F6).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE, m IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `served within` n `months of` d `by` m IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST x  THEN x AT LEAST d AND x AT MOST `the date` n `months from` d

§§ `Can a consumer redress order be made (ss 30G, 30K, 30N)`

-- s 30K(1): "the end of the period of 5 years from the time of the
-- contravention".
@ref s 30K(1)
GIVEN k IS A `Contravention facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the five years for` k MEANS `the date` 60 `months from` (k's `contravention on`)

-- s 30K(1)-(2): no final or provisional order — the order may be given by the
-- end of the five years, or later if before then the s 30I(1) notice or a
-- s 38(1) notice was served.
-- s 30K(3): a final or provisional order — only if the s 30I(1) notice is
-- served within 3 months from the confirmation or the making of the final
-- order, or within 6 months from the making of an unconfirmed provisional
-- order.
@ref s 30K
GIVEN k IS A `Contravention facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the time limits in s 30K are met for` k IF
    CONSIDER k's `the prior order`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
            k's `redress order made on` AT MOST five
        OR  `served on or before` (k's `section 30I notice served on`) `the date` five
        OR  `served on or before` (k's `section 38 notice served on`) `the date` five
    WHEN JUST (`a final order` d)                      THEN `served within` 3 `months of` d `by` (k's `section 30I notice served on`)
    WHEN JUST (`a confirmed provisional order` d)      THEN `served within` 3 `months of` d `by` (k's `section 30I notice served on`)
    WHEN JUST (`an unconfirmed provisional order` d)   THEN `served within` 6 `months of` d `by` (k's `section 30I notice served on`)
    WHERE
        five MEANS `the end of the five years for` k

@ref ss 30G(1), 30K, 30N(2), (4)
@export Can Ofgem (the Authority) make a consumer redress order for my supplier's contravention, under ss 30G, 30K and 30N of the Gas Act 1986 (UK)? The contravention must have caused me loss, damage or inconvenience; it must be after Schedule 14 to the Energy Act 2013 came into force; the Authority must not be satisfied that the Competition Act 1998 is the most appropriate way; and the time limits of s 30K must be met: 5 years from the contravention (unless a s 30I(1) or s 38(1) notice was served within them), or, after a final or provisional order, a s 30I(1) notice within 3 months of the final order or the confirmation, or 6 months of an unconfirmed provisional order. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN k IS A `Contravention facts`  @desc The contravention, its effect on me, any final or provisional order, the notices served, and the day of the order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a consumer redress order can be made for` k IF
        k's `I suffered loss, damage or inconvenience`
    AND k's `after Schedule 14 to the Energy Act 2013 came into force`
    AND NOT (k's `the Authority is satisfied the Competition Act 1998 is most appropriate`)
    AND `the time limits in s 30K are met for` k

§§ `Paying me under the order (ss 30G(5), 30M, 30N(1))`

-- s 30G(5): the compliance date "may not be earlier than the end of the
-- period of 7 days from the date of the service of a copy of the order on
-- the regulated person".
@ref s 30G(5)
GIVEN o IS A `Redress order facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the compliance date is lawful for` o IF
    o's `compliance date` AT LEAST `the date` 7 `days on from` (o's `copy served on the supplier on`)

-- s 30M(2): "within 42 days from the date of service on the regulated person
-- of a copy of the order".
@ref s 30M(2)
@export The supplier's last day to appeal against a consumer redress order to the court, under s 30M(2) of the Gas Act 1986 (UK): 42 days from the day a copy of the order was served on it. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN o IS A `Redress order facts`  @desc The day the copy of the order was served on the supplier
GIVETH A DATE
`the supplier's last day to appeal for` o MEANS
    `the date` 42 `days on from` (o's `copy served on the supplier on`)

-- s 30M(5): if an application is made, a requirement need not be carried out
-- until it has been determined.
@ref s 30M(5)
GIVEN o IS A `Redress order facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compliance is suspended by an appeal for` o IF
    CONSIDER o's `appeal made on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST a  THEN
            a AT MOST `the supplier's last day to appeal for` o
        AND o's `appeal determined on` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 30N(1): if compensation is not paid by the date required, the unpaid
-- balance carries interest at the Judgments Act 1838 rate — from the day
-- after that date.
@ref s 30N(1)
@export From what day does interest run on compensation under a consumer redress order that my supplier has not paid, under s 30N(1) of the Gas Act 1986 (UK)? The day after the compliance date, if the compensation is still unpaid then; NOTHING while an appeal suspends compliance (s 30M(5)) or if it was paid in time. The rate is that of s 17 of the Judgments Act 1838. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN o IS A `Redress order facts`  @desc The compliance date, any appeal, and the day the compensation was paid
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`interest on my compensation runs from` o MEANS
    IF     `compliance is suspended by an appeal for` o
        OR `served on or before` (o's `compensation paid on`) `the date` (o's `compliance date`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the date` 1 `days on from` (o's `compliance date`))

-- s 30O(2)-(4): compensation for a contravention may not exceed 10 per cent
-- of turnover, and with any penalty for it the total may not exceed 10 per
-- cent.
@ref s 30O(2)-(4)
@export The most compensation the supplier can be required to pay, in all, for one contravention, under s 30O of the Gas Act 1986 (UK): 10 per cent of its turnover, less any penalty imposed for the same contravention, and not below 0. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN o IS A `Redress order facts`  @desc The supplier's turnover and any penalty imposed for the contravention
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most compensation for the contravention under` o MEANS
    IF cap GREATER THAN 0 THEN cap ELSE 0
    WHERE
        cap MEANS 1/10 TIMES (o's `turnover`) MINUS (o's `penalty imposed`)

§§ `Gas resold to me (s 37)`

-- s 37(2)(b): where the reseller did not give the required information, the
-- maximum the direction substitutes. (4): the excess, and any interest the
-- direction provides for, are recoverable. (5): not for gas for a
-- gas-fuelled motor vehicle.
@ref s 37(2)(b), (4)-(5)
@export What can I recover from a person who resold gas to me above the maximum price, under s 37 of the Gas Act 1986 (UK)? The amount of the excess over the maximum price applicable (the reduced maximum where the reseller failed to give the information a direction requires), with any interest the direction provides for. NOTHING where s 37 does not apply (gas for a gas-fuelled motor vehicle). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Resale facts`  @desc The price paid, the maximum price and any reduced maximum, the interest under the direction, and whether the gas was for a motor vehicle
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`what I can recover on resale under` s MEANS
    IF s's `for a gas-fuelled motor vehicle`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF excess GREATER THAN 0
        THEN JUST (excess PLUS s's `interest under the direction`)
        ELSE JUST 0
    WHERE
        applicable MEANS
            CONSIDER s's `maximum price without the information`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN s's `maximum price`
            WHEN JUST m  THEN m
        excess MEANS s's `price paid` MINUS applicable
